many discontinuities on this closed interval.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ only.\"" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348575 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348576 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348577 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348578 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348579 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1041 "selection" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348579 13194139535424 true] [17592186348574 1110 #uuid "73da814f-3f52-51d9-ac85-be27daa4b0b5" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348575 1034 "$f,g$ and $h$" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348575 1111 #uuid "2a5b835b-dad5-53f7-b678-f6af10b37644" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348576 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348576 1111 #uuid "f4cd65e6-ca79-5c48-bf1a-94cad2c908db" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348577 1034 "$h$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348577 1111 #uuid "e152bfac-5686-591e-998e-12ea0e487194" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348578 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348578 1111 #uuid "bc5f2fb4-c974-556f-b4b7-47dc2f39de8c" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348579 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348579 1111 #uuid "19a9c2a4-659a-51c6-8d02-7a7ddfd858d2" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348581 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1089 "q-394135" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1100 "Which of the following functions are piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1]?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4x-3, & x<0 \\\\ -2x+5, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,,\\,g(x)={x}^{3}-\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}},\\,h(x)={x}^{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}\n$$" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1113 #uuid "28afde2c-2363-58b2-8a4a-6ad2f7d5c5ed" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348580 1145 "A function $f(x)$ is **piecewise smooth** on $x\\in [a,b]$ if\n\n- $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous on $[a,b],$ and\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists and is continuous except possibly at finitely many points, where its one-sided limits exist and are finite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0.$ On each open interval, $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the function is linear. On these intervals,\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4x-3, & x<0 \\\\ -2x+5, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\,,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={\\begin{aligned}4, & x<0 \\\\ -2, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ are piecewise continuous on each open interval, and they both have finite limits at the endpoints of the subintervals.\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{3}-\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0$ into the two open intervals $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1).$ For $x\\ne 0,$\n\n$$\ng(x)={x}^{3}-{x}^{3/5},\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{2/5}}.\n$$\n\nWhile this derivative is continuous on the open pieces $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the limits of the derivative as $x\\to 0$ are not finite. In fact, the derivative becomes unbounded near $x=0.$ Thus, the condition for finite limits at the endpoints is not met.\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{10/3},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{10}{3}{x}^{7/3}.\n$$\n\nHere, $h(x)$ and ${h}^{′}(x)$ are continuous on $[-1,1].$ Thus, $h(x)$ is continuously differentiable on the whole interval, and hence piecewise smooth.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ and $h$ only.\"" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348582 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348583 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348584 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348585 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348586 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1041 "selection" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348586 13194139535424 true] [17592186348581 1110 #uuid "8c4a66b7-2bc6-5bb7-a851-b66aebcb93b5" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348582 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348582 1111 #uuid "c8e87d3f-c3c7-53e8-9718-a515e0b6f4cb" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348583 1034 "$h$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348583 1111 #uuid "3c1043e8-53c9-53ab-b8f0-769de56754e8" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348584 1034 "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348584 1111 #uuid "00784f4d-6616-535b-84e9-7f4d6076547a" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348585 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348585 1111 #uuid "eec44f55-5355-5837-9219-b4e4990d8e05" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348586 1034 "$f$ and $h$ only" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535424 true] [17592186348586 1111 #uuid "8bbfd531-cf72-5e56-8119-b4219fdd1c18" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348588 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1089 "q-394140" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1100 "Which of the following functions are piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1]?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4x-1, & x<0 \\\\ 4x+3, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,,\\,g(x)={x}^{2}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}},\\,h(x)={x}^{2}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}\n$$" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1113 #uuid "344f57b8-c115-5f45-be4c-e3f3ba12bb83" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348587 1145 "A function $f(x)$ is **piecewise smooth** on $x\\in [a,b]$ if\n\n- $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous on $[a,b],$ and\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists and is continuous except possibly at finitely many points, where its one-sided limits exist and are finite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0.$ On each open interval, $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the function is linear. On these intervals,\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4x-1, & x<0 \\\\ 4x+3, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\,,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={\\begin{aligned}4, & x<0 \\\\ 4, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ are piecewise continuous on each open interval, and they both have finite limits at the endpoints of the subintervals.\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{2}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since\n\n$$\ng(x)={x}^{2}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}={x}^{2}+{x}^{4/3},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)=2x+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nHere, $g(x)$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ are continuous on $[-1,1].$ Thus, $g(x)$ is continuously differentiable on the whole interval, and hence piecewise smooth.\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{2}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{2}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}={x}^{14/5},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{14}{5}{x}^{9/5}.\n$$\n\nHere, $h(x)$ and ${h}^{′}(x)$ are continuous on $[-1,1].$ Thus, $h(x)$ is continuously differentiable on the whole interval, and hence piecewise smooth.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f,$ $g,$ and $h.$\"" 13194139535424 true] [17592186348588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348589 13194139535424 true] [17592186348588 1000 